Patch already-present but unpatched packages on every sync, not just new installs.

The per-wheel hook from 02-uv-crate-nix-dispatch.patch only runs inside
execute_plan, for the wheels installed in that run. Every "nothing to do"
path skips it: the sync fast path (finish_noop), the empty-plan branch in
InstallationPlan::execute, `uv pip install` when requirements are already
satisfied, ephemeral environments that are already fresh, and reused tool
environments. So a package that was installed by a stock uv, by an older
uv-nix, or by an interrupted run stayed unpatched until someone ran
`uv nix patch` by hand.

nix_reconcile calls uv_nix::reconcile_venv on each of those paths. It is a
single read_dir compared against <venv>/share/uv-nix/processed.json, so a
fully patched environment pays almost nothing.

